    "Platinum reads more like Mac OS 9, and Classic's radio buttons and checkboxes show again. Window frames, scroll bars, desktop and Apple-menu icons, the Control Strip, and the small text in lists, labels and status bars follow real Mac OS 9 screens. Bold titles, buttons and menus keep a bold face, because Geneva has none. Reading and editing text keep their modern sizes. In Classic, some installs had blank radio buttons and checkboxes, so the Control Panel's AI Connection list showed only labels; they show again.",
